The Archive is a library reached through the threshold in the Threshold Expeditions office of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]]. It is dead. [[Divinity/The Narrative/Mike|Mike]], one of the [[Divinity/The Narrative/index|Narrative]], killed it, and what the threshold leads into now is its decaying corpse: one great heap of rotted books under a dark open space, with the bodies of an Oreskian expedition scattered through the pile. The expedition went in without knowing what waited there, and the Archive took what they knew; some of what they carried still lies where they fell, and the violet keycard of the facility was taken off one of them. The Archive was known to the [[People/Althane/The Broker|Broker]]. Others have moved into the corpse and live there. When strangers come, loose books rise off the heap and stack themselves into a man-shaped figure, and worse things come up out of the ink.

The dead library beyond the threshold was not a building but the body of a good [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]], whose form was all the books that ever existed; it is not really a Thessian anymore. [[People/Althane/The Broker|The Broker]] carries the body now, tethered to him, and draws from it what his people know of books. [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Harrow|The Harrow]] made off with the part of its portfolio that was knowledge, and the Broker kept what he could so that it could not swallow the whole.

Before it died, Archive was the sixth floor of the [[Geography/Ushas/Undermountain|Undermountain]] on [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]]: an endless and exceptionally dangerous repository of all the knowledge on Ushas, which could be summoned anywhere on Ushas where enough books were gathered in one place. It aided the party that would found [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] with knowledge in its own way, and they learned only from [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Dragon|Dragon]] that it was a Thessian. Its library's knowledge went into Sedecium's founding.
